Robotiq Hand-E gripper description — provenance and licence
============================================================

meshes/*.stl and the kinematics of robotiq_hande.xml (link and joint names, axes, travel, finger and
body offsets) are derived from Robotiq's own ROS 2 description package `robotiq_description`
(version 1.3.0):

  repository : https://github.com/robotiq/ros
  commit     : c39cd970a3f950c8be206d0e4340c7b69e018d7a
  meshes     : grippers/robotiq_description/meshes/visual/hand_e/{hand-e,left_finger,right_finger}.dae
  kinematics : grippers/robotiq_description/urdf/robotiq_hand_e_macro.urdf.xacro

The meshes were converted from Collada to STL by external/convert/convert_robotiq_hande_meshes.py;
their vertices are unchanged. The GRP-CPL-062 coupling, which that package does not model, is drawn
as a plain disc of its published size. The collision geometry is primitives fitted to the finger
meshes, and the masses, centre of mass, inertia, grip force and finger speed are taken from Robotiq's
Hand-E instruction manual for Universal Robots, revision 2022/01/10 (see the comments in
robotiq_hande.xml).

